@startuml Register

title Register API Sequence

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Registration Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
participant "API" as api
participant "Application" as app
participant "Domain" as domain
participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
database "m_user" as m_user
database "t_consent" as t_consent
database "m_consent_type" as m_consent_type
database "m_user_password" as m_user_password
database "m_user_information" as m_user_information
database "t_user_address" as t_user_address
database "t_user_consent" as t_user_consent
database "l_user_referral" as l_user_referral
end box
user -> page: Enter registration; view consent versions
activate page
page -> api: POST v1/auth/register over TLS\n(content-type, timestamp, requestId, body)
activate api
api -> app: [**RegisterCommandHandler**] Process RegisterCommand
activate app
    note over app, infra
        Lock order: this endpoint creates a new user and takes no pre-existing user FOR UPDATE lock. All writes use
        that new userId; repeated child consent writes are ordered by consentId. The REPEATABLE READ snapshot provides
        consistent policy reads; existing uniqueness/FK constraints remain authoritative for concurrent
        writes/deletions. A concurrent referenced-row deletion yielding FK violation rolls back and returns 404
        E10005. Retry serialization conflicts as a whole; never bypass constraints or update existing consent history.
    end note
app -> app: Create request context; generate requestId if omitted
app -> domain: Validate headers, JSON, scalar/object types, password policy, unique consentIds
domain -> app: Return input validation
alt Invalid input
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Validation error
else Valid input
    app -> app: Encrypt sensitive fields; random 16 byte salt; PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 600,000 iterations
    app -> app: createdBy = auth-register; preserve input identifier representation
    app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ
    note over app, infra
        Capture UTC now immediately before the first read; that first read establishes the transaction snapshot. All
        consent/type/referrer reads and duplicate checks use this same snapshot. Capture no new policy snapshot
        halfway through registration. A consent/type/version published after that snapshot is handled as pending for
        the resulting existing user (Q9); registration does not promise to accept an unseen publication at commit
        time. A serialization conflict rolls back and retries the entire transaction with a new snapshot/now and
        freshly revalidated inputs, bounded by the request timeout; no partial retry or partial writes.
        `referrerId`, if present, must be a UUID referencing an existing user in the transaction snapshot (any
        lifecycle status; the existing referral relationship is historical, not a privilege grant). Missing
        reference returns the same 404 E10005. Omission creates no referral row. Register never grants
        PLATFORM_ADMIN from an email or referrer.
    end note
    alt Transaction work completes
        app -> app: Capture UTC now immediately before first read; establish one snapshot
        app -> infra: QUERY - Check existing user
        infra -> m_user: QUERY - Check existing user
        activate m_user
            note right of m_user
                SELECT
                    u.id as user_id
                FROM authen.m_user u
                WHERE (u.username = '<sequence.usernameBytes>' OR u.email_address = '<sequence.emailAddressBytes>')
            end note
            m_user -> infra: Return matching existing user ids
        deactivate m_user
        infra -> app: Return matching existing user ids
        alt Existing username or email
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 Username or email address already exists.
            api -> page: Duplicate identifier
        else No existing identifier
            app -> infra: QUERY - Get effective consents
            infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get effective consents
            activate t_consent
                note right of t_consent
                    SELECT
                        c.id as consent_id,
                        c.consent_type_id,
                        c.consent_version,
                        c.is_required
                    FROM consent.t_consent c
                    WHERE c.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    AND c.effective_at <= '<sequence.now>'
                    AND (c.expired_at IS NULL OR c.expired_at > '<sequence.now>')
                    ORDER BY c.id
                end note
                t_consent -> infra: Return effectiveConsents (consentId, typeId, version, isRequired)
            deactivate t_consent
            infra -> app: Return effectiveConsents (consentId, typeId, version, isRequired)
            app -> app: consentTypeIds = distinct effectiveConsents.consent_type_id
            app -> infra: QUERY - Get active consent types
            infra -> m_consent_type: QUERY - Get active consent types
            activate m_consent_type
                note right of m_consent_type
                    SELECT
                        ct.id as consent_type_id
                    FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                    WHERE ct.id = ANY ('<sequence.consentTypeIds>'::UUID[])
                    AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    ORDER BY ct.id
                end note
                m_consent_type -> infra: Return activeTypeIds
            deactivate m_consent_type
            infra -> app: Return activeTypeIds
            app -> app: applicableConsents = effectiveConsents with typeId in activeTypeIds
            alt referrerId is specified
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check referrer
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Check referrer
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as referrer_id
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = '<sequence.referrerId>' -- only when referrerId is specified
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return referrer id or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return referrer id or no row
                app -> app: referenceValid = referrer row returned
            else referrerId omitted
                app -> app: referenceValid = true; no referral write
            end
            app -> domain: Validate submitted ids/versions and all applicable required acceptances
            domain -> app: Return reference, version and required-coverage validation
            alt Missing/hidden consent or missing referrer
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 Consent or referrer not found.
                api -> page: Reference invalid
            else Displayed consentVersion differs from current version
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 Consent version is no longer current.
                api -> page: Reload current consents
            else Required consent missing or result is not explicit true
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 All current required consents must be accepted.
                api -> page: Required acceptance missing
            else All references, versions and required acceptances valid
                app -> infra: INSERT - Create user
                infra -> m_user: INSERT - Create user
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        INSERT INTO authen.m_user (
                            created_by,
                            username,
                            email_address,
                            first_name,
                            last_name,
                            display_name,
                            profile_picture_path
                        )
                        VALUES (
                            &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                            &#39;<sequence.usernameBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.emailAddressBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.firstNameBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.lastNameBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.displayName>',
                            &#39;<sequence.profilePicturePath>'
                        )
                        RETURNING id as user_id
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return new user_id
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return new user_id
                app -> app: userId = returned user_id; all children use this server-derived id
                app -> infra: INSERT - Create password
                infra -> m_user_password: INSERT - Create password
                activate m_user_password
                    note right of m_user_password
                        INSERT INTO authen.m_user_password (
                            created_by,
                            row_type,
                            user_id,
                            password,
                            password_salt
                        )
                        VALUES (
                            &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                            &#39;PASSWORD',
                            &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                            &#39;<sequence.passwordBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.passwordSaltBytes>'
                        )
                    end note
                    m_user_password -> infra: Return one PASSWORD row inserted
                deactivate m_user_password
                infra -> app: Return one PASSWORD row inserted
                app -> infra: INSERT - Create user information
                infra -> m_user_information: INSERT - Create user information
                activate m_user_information
                    note right of m_user_information
                        INSERT INTO authen.m_user_information (
                            created_by,
                            user_id,
                            phone_number,
                            address,
                            date_of_birth,
                            gender
                        )
                        VALUES (
                            &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                            &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                            &#39;<sequence.phoneNumberBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.addressBytes>',
                            &#39;<sequence.dateOfBirth>',
                            &#39;<sequence.gender>'
                        )
                    end note
                    m_user_information -> infra: Return one information row inserted
                deactivate m_user_information
                infra -> app: Return one information row inserted
                alt addresses object supplied
                    app -> infra: INSERT - Create user address
                    infra -> t_user_address: INSERT - Create user address
                    activate t_user_address
                        note right of t_user_address
                            INSERT INTO authen.t_user_address (
                                created_by,
                                user_id,
                                title,
                                is_default,
                                address,
                                city,
                                state,
                                postal_code,
                                country
                            )
                            VALUES (
                                &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.title>',
                                TRUE, -- the first address of a user is the default address, whatever isDefault says
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.addressBytes>',
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.cityBytes>',
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.stateBytes>',
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.postalCodeBytes>',
                                &#39;<sequence.addresses.countryBytes>'
                            )
                        end note
                        t_user_address -> infra: Return default address inserted
                    deactivate t_user_address
                    infra -> app: Return default address inserted
                else addresses omitted
                    app -> app: No address row
                end
                alt Validated consents list is non-empty
                    loop Each supplied consent ordered by consentId
                        app -> app: Bind displayed consentVersion; result = explicit result or false; isRead = true; readAt = now
                        app -> infra: INSERT - Create user consent
                        infra -> t_user_consent: INSERT - Create user consent
                        activate t_user_consent
                            note right of t_user_consent
                                INSERT INTO authen.t_user_consent (
                                    created_by,
                                    user_id,
                                    consent_id,
                                    consent_version,
                                    result,
                                    is_read,
                                    read_at
                                )
                                VALUES (
                                    &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.consents.consentId>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.consents.consentVersion>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.consents.result>', -- explicit result, or false when omitted
                                    TRUE, -- supplied object records displayed/read version
                                    &#39;<sequence.now>'
                                )
                            end note
                            t_user_consent -> infra: Return read consent evidence inserted
                        deactivate t_user_consent
                        infra -> app: Return read consent evidence inserted
                    end loop
                else No supplied consents
                    app -> app: No consent evidence rows
                end
                alt Validated referrerId supplied
                    app -> infra: INSERT - Create user referral
                    infra -> l_user_referral: INSERT - Create user referral
                    activate l_user_referral
                        note right of l_user_referral
                            INSERT INTO authen.l_user_referral (
                                created_by,
                                user_id,
                                referrer_id
                            )
                            VALUES (
                                &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                &#39;<sequence.referrerId>'
                            )
                        end note
                        l_user_referral -> infra: Return referral inserted
                    deactivate l_user_referral
                    infra -> app: Return referral inserted
                else No referrer
                    app -> app: No referral row
                end
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed registration
                note over app, infra
                    If present, title/address/city/state/postalCode/country must be non-empty strings, title at most 128
                    characters, and isDefault if present must be boolean. The first address is always default: SQL sets TRUE
                    whatever isDefault says. Omission creates no address row. The separate top-level address remains the
                    optional profile field.
                    Each supplied item must contain a UUID consentId and a non-empty consentVersion of at most 8 characters;
                    result if present must be boolean. Reject duplicate consentIds before SQL (400 E10001), rather than picking
                    one answer. Do not default the version to 1.0.0 or the latest version. Required consent needs explicit
                    result=true; false or omission is not acceptance.
                    Read all currently effective ACTIVE consents (effective_at <= now and expired_at IS NULL or expired_at >
                    now), then only their ACTIVE consent types. Keep consent rows whose consent_type_id belongs to that
                    activeTypeIds set. Required means `t_consent.is_required`, not the type's is_required flag. Do not require
                    or accept an expired, future, inactive or inactive-type consent. Empty id lists bind as empty UUID arrays,
                    never IN ().
                    Display/read semantics (Q16): every supplied valid consent object represents the displayed version, even
                    with result omitted. Insert is_read=TRUE and read_at=now. Map omitted result to false only for this new
                    registration evidence; explicit false is an optional rejection. Omitted optional consent creates no row and
                    stays pending. The authenticated submit endpoint uses the same read-only/result distinction after
                    registration; repeated reads preserve the first read_at and any answer, as specified separately in its own
                    review.
                    The username and email address must not exist yet in their respective columns, across every lifecycle state,
                    otherwise 409 E10003 `Username or email address already exists.` Their existing separate UNIQUE constraints
                    are final protection against concurrent registrations: SQLSTATE 23505 from either m_user identifier
                    constraint rolls back the whole transaction and maps to that same 409. Other integrity failures are not
                    mislabeled as duplicates. Cross-field username/email collisions remain possible and login rejects ambiguous
                    matching accounts (Q14).
                    After every validation succeeds: create user, take returned user_id as userId, create exactly one PASSWORD
                    row and one information row, then optional address, supplied consent rows in consentId order, and optional
                    referral. createdBy is the server service identifier `auth-register`, not request input. Bind omitted
                    nullable scalars as SQL NULL, never the string 'null'; bind bytes, UUIDs, booleans and timestamps as typed
                    values. All placeholders below are parameter notation, never interpolated SQL.
                    COMMIT must succeed before returning 201 S10000 with data.userId. Failure of password, information, address,
                    any consent or referral insertion rolls back user and every child together. Timeout before commit rolls back
                    and returns 408 E90001. Unexpected pre-commit failure rolls back and returns generic 500 without inventing a
                    bizCode. A lost response after commit does not undo registration: the client may encounter 409 on retry and
                    should use login. No registration write is intentionally durable on a failed pre-commit response.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 201 S10000 Register Success; data.userId = userId
                api -> page: Return userId only
                page -> user: Registered; proceed to login
            end
        end
    else m_user identifier UNIQUE violation SQLSTATE 23505
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 Username or email address already exists.
        api -> page: Concurrent duplicate
    else Referenced row deleted concurrently; FK violation
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 Consent or referrer not found.
        api -> page: Reference no longer exists
    else Serialization conflict
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> app: Retry whole transaction with new snapshot/now within request timeout
        ref over app, infra
            Repeat validation reads and all writes; never retry a partial transaction
            End with the corresponding success/error path; exhaustion follows timeout below
        end ref
    else Timeout before COMMIT
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
        api -> page: Timeout; no partial registration
    else Unexpected failure before COMMIT
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
        api -> page: Generic failure; no partial registration
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
